+// ---- frame interpolation (--interpolate) ----------------------------------------------------------
+// The game draws 30 frames a second; the screen shows 60. Each frame's
+// record is kept, and once a frame is complete (its XFB copy) it is drawn
+// a second time, before it is shown, as the frame halfway from the one
+// before: each draw found in the frame before (by what it draws: primitive,
+// vertex format and count, textures, matrix) gets its matrices (position,
+// texture, normal, projection) halfway between the two frames', and its
+// vertices too when they moved on the CPU (skinning). What is not found,
+// or moved too far (a cut), is drawn where it is. The halfway frame has
+// its own EFB and EFB copies, and the game's state is untouched by it: it
+// is shown at one retrace and the real frame at the next, a retrace later
+// than without (17 ms). The game itself runs exactly as before.
+constexpr uint32_t XI_POS = 0x100, XI_NRM = 0x60, XI_PRJ = 7, XI_WORDS = XI_POS + XI_NRM + XI_PRJ;
